  <figure>
    <img src="/assets/images/area-history/1960s/310-1960-ambulance.jpg" alt="Historic image from the Grooving through the Sixties 1960-1969 page">
  </figure>
</div>

<p>In August, the Mandan City Commission voted to support an ambulance service for the city by joining in a three-party contract with the Bismarck Ambulance Service to provide an ambulance and driver for the city of Mandan. Current “ambulance” operators, Warren Buehler of Buehler Funeral Home and Hector Hoenig of Hoenig Funeral Home had announced earlier this year their intention to suspend their services.</p>

<p>Suffering through one of the most severe droughts in recent history, local farmers saw crop yields drop by about a third compared to typical yields.</p>

<h3>1969</h3>

<p>In October 1969, Cass-Clay Creameries of Fargo purchased the operation of Foremost Dairies in Mandan. The sale, for an undisclosed sum, was prompted by the far distances from their other operations in the southwest and west coast of the nation.</p>
